        "original_id": "d3927a36-6396-59a2-9350-b2207f1f9676",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Len Reynolds, H. V. Evatt, Sir Edmund Barton, Bill Arthur\n- Organizations: Australian Labor Party, Liberal Party\n- Places: Division of Barton, New South Wales, Australia\n- Roles: party leader, Prime Minister\n- Topics: Australian electoral divisions, federal elections\n\nFacts:\n- The Division of Barton is an Australian electoral division in the state of New South Wales.\n- The Division of Barton was created in 1922 and was named for Sir Edmund Barton, the first Prime Minister of Australia.\n- In 1958, Len Reynolds was selected as the Australian Labor Party candidate for the seat of Barton after party leader H. V. Evatt left the seat because it was perceived to be too marginal.\n- In 1966, Bill Arthur defeated Labor member Len Reynolds and was elected for the Liberal Party.",
